static lstr L3865 = {0, 5, "E0611"};
static lstr L3866 = {0, 192, "An arrow function takes its parameter types from the function type it is passed to. With no expected type, each parameter needs a written type.\012Fix: `(x) => x + 1` becomes `(x: int) => x + 1`."};
static lstr L3867 = {0, 5, "E0612"};
static lstr L3868 = {0, 279, "A closure can capture a `let` variable only when it is passed straight to a function parameter that is not escaping. A stored or returned closure may run after the variable is gone.\012Fix: capture a `const` copy of the value, or keep the changing value in a `Cell` from `std/cell`."};
static lstr L3869 = {0, 5, "E0613"};
static lstr L3870 = {0, 239, "A closure can capture a `mutable` parameter only when it is passed straight to a function parameter that is not escaping. The same holds for a loop element changed in place.\012Fix: copy the value first with `copy(name)` and capture the copy."};
static lstr L3871 = {0, 5, "E0614"};
static lstr L3872 = {0, 255, "A closure passed to this call assigns the variable while the call runs. The other arguments are passed by reference, so the function could read the variable while the closure changes it.\012Fix: read the variable into a `const` before the call and pass that."};
static lstr L3873 = {0, 5, "E0615"};
static lstr L3874 = {0, 233, "A generator runs its body each time it is resumed, after the call that created it has returned. So a function parameter of a generator must be `escaping`.\012Fix: `function* g(f: () => int)` becomes `function* g(escaping f: () => int)`."};
static lstr L3875 = {0, 5, "E0700"};
static lstr L3876 = {0, 253, "In a pattern, a name that starts with a capital letter is a constructor, and a lowercase name binds the value. The value here has no constructor with this name.\012Fix: write the binding in lowercase, or match a value of the enum that has this constructor."};
